# The fixed-width integers: a word of width w is w booleans in nested cells, the least
# significant first, ending in word_end, so the width is the depth of the
# value's structure. Every operation takes the width, a natural, as its first
# argument and recurses on it, and wraps to the width by keeping the length:
# two's complement overflow is the definition itself. One set of defines and
# lemmas serves every width; int32_* and int16_* are thin defines naming the
# instances at 32 and 16. Compiled with native_types. The defines are the
# lambdalattice files of the directory fixed_width/. Each operation reads
# every intermediate word once, since a reading that does not share
# computes a word read twice twice (word_multiply's comment has the
# measurement).
#
# The schemes, Name = Name + (Name ∥ T), absorption, as native_types writes
# them, each over the operation applied to its width W, a metavariable, so
# that one lemma serves every width: the term `word_add @ W` is the body of
# the thin define int32_add at W = int32_width.
